From e702afd5ce1007e19e751503e7a49985a3905893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jozsef Kiraly <fonix232@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:21:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] qualcommax: ipq807x: add QNAP 301w (OpenWrt U-Boot
 layout)

A second variant of the QNAP 301w for units whose eMMC has been
converted to the OpenWrt U-Boot layout: our U-Boot (chainloaded from the
stock one, later in place of it) and two firmware slots, each holding a
FIT and, after it, that slot's own overlay:

  0:HLOS       4 MiB   U-Boot loader FIT (chainload stage)
  0:HLOS_1     4 MiB   second copy of the loader (stock U-Boot fallback)
  ubootenv     1 MiB   U-Boot environment, primary copy
  ubootenv2    1 MiB   U-Boot environment, redundant copy
  fit_a      512 MiB   slot A: FIT (kernel, DTB, squashfs), then overlay
  fit_b      512 MiB   slot B
  data         rest    shared storage, not an overlay

The slot FITs carry the squashfs as external data and are mounted with
fitblk, which maps the rest of the slot as /dev/fitrw for fstools'
overlay. U-Boot selects the slot by copying /chosen/rootdisk-a or
rootdisk-b to /chosen/rootdisk. A sysupgrade writes the slot that is not
running, puts the settings into that slot's overlay area, and only then
switches boot_slot; U-Boot's boot counter falls back to the previous
slot, with its own untouched overlay, if the new one does not come up,
and the bootcount init script marks a successful boot.

Images use configuration config@hk01 so that the stock U-Boot can boot
them too (recovery). Enable CONFIG_UIMAGE_FIT_BLK for the target.
